2019's escape room is a wild ride with a  bonkers ending  and you can say the same for its 2021  sequel tournament of champions  from mysterious planes to the meaning  behind those strange shipping containers  this is the ending of escape room  tournament of champions explained  at the end of 2019's escape room we  learn that the evil minos organization  behind the movie's killer game  chose each participant for their status  as a sole survivor  of various disasters as the game's  master at the end of the first movie put  it they wanted to  know if luck had anything to do with it  tournament of champions introduces a  host of new characters who like ben and  zoe  have done this dance before none are  particularly keen on repeating the  experience  soon enough we learn about the qualities  that got these characters sucked into  mino's  machinations in the first place rachel  can't feel physical pain  and likely face horrifying psychological  torture during her game  briana survived a game featuring notable  influences  nathan entered the game with fellow  priests to test his faith  by picking specific groups of people  minos wants to test hypotheses about  faith  pain fame empathy and survival they  don't care who gets hurt in the process  and if it makes them a hefty sum of  money all the better  while many things still aren't clear at  the end of 2019's escape room we can  say with certainty that zoe and ben  aren't still trapped in an escape room  when they leave the first game alive  but their victory is still short-lived  as we then see minos operatives planning  what seems to be their next game with  zoe and ben's intercepted flight  information  so while the two champions may be back  to their old lives that doesn't mean  minos isn't still watching them  and given the number of people involved  in the airplane testing at the first  film's close it's safe to say that minos  isn't exactly a small time operation  it's clear that minos has people in the  real world manipulating things from the  outside  whether they're directly involved in ben  and zoe's lives or placed on the  outskirts to watch and report back  furthermore minos is capable of both  hijacking a plane and a subway train  one private company can't do that  without some high level connections no  matter how evil they are  what's more since we don't see most of  the dead characters actually die  there's no telling which players might  have been mino's double agents from the  start  the players first suspect ben after all  could they have been right all along  or is someone else pulling the strings  the deaths of the first film seem pretty  cut and dry by the time that story draws  to a close  but in light of the events of tournament  of champions we have to question  everything  if amanda can survive hurtling into an  endless abyss who's to say that other  apparently deceased characters didn't  also cheat death  and which ones might have been involved  with minos from the jump  in tournament of champions we're led to  believe that everyone except zoe amanda  and ben bite the dust  but how true is that really as amanda  tells zoe if she didn't see the deaths  herself they didn't happen  since rachel checks out theo's  electrocuted body to determine he's  actually dead he's the likeliest actual  casualty  but the other deaths are murkier after  nathan saves rachel from quicksand he  sinks to his presumed death  but that's how we initially lose ben too  we later discover ben survived to serve  as leverage for zoe to follow minos's  bidding  it wouldn't be surprising if nathan  survived too then  that brings us to rachel and brianna we  watch as a monsoon of acid rain assaults  them  but the film quickly cuts to zoe  freaking out the steam and smoke make it  impossible  to tell what really happens to them  which could be another trick  as amanda says if you didn't see it it  didn't happen so are they really gone  what the heck is going on with amanda  she shows up out of the blue toward the  end of the movie  claiming minos forced her into designing  the game that zoe just played  that's an interesting sentiment for her  to express considering amanda doesn't  come close to beating the game in the  first film  as an evil organization minos doesn't  seem likely to applaud anything less  than first place  and amanda was one of the first few  casualties in the 2019 film  while it's reasonable to believe that  minos might force her into designing the  latest game  especially since the game appears to be  plan b it's just as likely that our  innocent amanda has been amino's plant  all along  while amanda has mentioned her daughter  we never actually see any flashback  clips with amanda and sonia  we do however see amanda's time as a  soldier alongside the other characters  flashback sequences in the first film  the culmination of events at the end of  the film feels way too easy as zoe knows  it's entirely possible that amanda isn't  who she says she is  for all we know her daughter sonja is a  total fabrication  invented to hoodwink zoe into  cooperation  a massive display of huge shipping  containers can be glimpsed when the  characters escape the creepy bedroom  they're labeled nyc bdrm bch  and bnk these letters seem likely to be  shorthand for new york city  bedroom beach and bank in shorts the  escape rooms minos throws the characters  into during the scow round  at the top of course is our lone subway  car we also see a painting of an eight  ball  hinting that the original escape rooms  might be in this underground bunker as  well  the games have to exist somewhere of  course but the scope of the subway car  and the nyc room is mind-boggling  zoe and ben appear to get on a real  subway platform and a real q train  as we see it dislodged at the beginning  of the movie that's a massive feat to  pull off  any new yorker can tell you that the mta  is a hot mess on a good day  but building hiding and or inserting an  extra track wouldn't exactly go  unnoticed  to say nothing of how minos lord the  other champions onto this particular car  without anyone else hopping on  the fact that minos pulls off the subway  heights of the century speaks to the  connections and tech they have at their  disposal  but it also tells us that reality isn't  always what it seems  the subway car is likely a mix of  reality and a few minos adjustments but  what about the police station  when zoe and ben are on their doomed  flight and zoe questions how easy it all  seems ben says  you really think the whole police  station was bull yes ben  yes we do if there really was a raid on  minos's extracurricular activities  the involved parties would be  hightailing it to a country without  extradition loss  not throwing together another deadly  escape room so it seems like everything  else that the news broadcasts about four  found bodies and the manhunt is  fabricated  that means a guy who steals zoe's bag  and compass at the beginning of the film  is amino's plant who lures zoe and ben  into the specific subway car that also  means his arrest is an illusion  given how massive the police station is  this conspiracy goes dramatically deep  a staggering number of people must be on  the mino's payroll  there are probably multiple cops pulling  the strings and hiding evidence amino  says behest  it's too big of an enterprise not to  have those kinds of connections in place  while killer planes are certainly scary  learning a trusted ally is in fact a  manipulative liar is even scarier  when someone talks to a therapist they  expose their vulnerabilities  to learn that their therapist is  destabilizing their concept of reality  would be devastating  someone with deep rooted btsd from being  trapped in a killer escape room would be  especially shaken by this  while it's not abundantly clear that  zoe's therapist is involved with minos  there are some pretty shady coincidences  surrounding her  first off there's a lighthouse painting  in the therapist's office which  foreshadows the beach escape room  then at the start of the film the  therapist encourages zoe to take the  trip to nyc with ben  that's not entirely damning on its own  part of a therapist's job is helping  patients work through trauma  to achieve some level of normalcy let's  call this an orange flag then  not quite a red flag but not green  either from there things get worse  minos originally plans on hoodwinking  ben and zoe with a hijacked flight  they move to plan b when zoey can't  bring herself to get on the plane  what's plan b oh just a commandeer  subway car and what's the title of the  book the therapist brandishes at zoey  while accusing her  of finding clues in everything it was  called free will how to stop the train  of negative thinking  that's a little too much of a  coincidence to not be a clue  it's difficult to say for sure what  exactly goes down in tournament of  champions  due to minos's love of deception and  digital trickery  the why however isn't so muddy the  escape room franchise might bear  similarities to horror titles like cube  and soar  but tournament of champions has a hunger  games vibe specifically the hunger games  catching fire just as that film forces  previous hunger games winners to do  battle  tournament of champions pits those who  have survived mino's escape room  against each other the motivation for  the games in both film series is simple  the wealthy view everyone who isn't part  of their high-class circle as  entertaining playthings and the hunger  games the bloodthirsty elite are the  denizens of the capital  in the escape room movies it's whoever's  paying for a front row seat to menos  deadly games  they say that money can't buy happiness  but apparently it can buy  gladiator-style death matches  through this the escape room series  critiques societal stratification  and the way wealth corrupts morality as  well as offering a glimpse of the  horrific things people can do with  technology  if they're so cruelly inclined our  customers are some of the most  powerful people in the world but every  year they demand more  among all of the perks privilege can buy  is anonymity  minos and all of its wealthy patrons are  able to remain unknown  they hide behind their technology  torturing kids for fun from an ivory  tower while everyone else gets their  hands dirty  in contrast zoe and ben don't have the  luxury of disappearing behind the dollar  sign  the escape room movies deeply explore  what it means to be a survivor  and the lens to which someone will go to  save themselves who will fight for  others the series asks and who will  simply save their own life  the premise of the first film hinges  entirely on survival  each and willing participants soul  survivor background tells me knows  something about who they are  whether it's jason killing his best  friend or ben drunkenly but  unintentionally killing his friends on a  car crash but something about zoe saving  ben  continues to peak minos interest while  the rest of the champions games seems to  have been one and done experiments  minos remains fixated on the concept of  the survivor  why else would they throw previous  survivors in one ring to duke it out yet  again  the rest of the survivors appear to be  cannon fudder as minos sight remains  fixed on zoe  and their desire for her to build them a  new game zoe continues to survive  despite the criminally low odds of  living through the game  this makes her the perfect person to  design a genuinely unbeatable escape  room sequence  but she'll never agree to it more so we  think  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

